00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:54.950
Come on.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:56.810
Don't you guys want to know what's going on?

00:21:58.740 --> 00:21:59.140
Okay.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:03.330
Okay. Where do we hide?

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:10.240
Over there.

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:17.280
We should be able to see from here.

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:37.180
I hope we don't see anything we don't want to see.

00:22:37.690 --> 00:22:41.720
Like Tom and Huck at the trial of Muff Potter.

00:22:42.030 --> 00:22:45.890
Only Tom, Huck, and Crazy Joe knew what had really happened in the graveyard.

00:22:46.580 --> 00:22:50.260
Do you solemnly swear to tell the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the truth, so help you God?

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:51.980
Yes, sir, I do.

00:22:56.170 --> 00:22:59.800
Joe, you were at the graveyard on the 17th of June.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:00.540
At midnight?

00:23:01.240 --> 00:23:01.740
Yes.

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:06.000
So you saw the defendant stab the young Dr. Robinson with this knife?

00:23:06.810 --> 00:23:09.320
Yes, sir. Sad to say I did.

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:14.690
The defendant has admitted that this knife, the murder weapon, belonged to him.

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:17.470
Is this the knife that you saw him use?

00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:20.440
Sir, as I'm sitting here, it is the very knife.

00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:22.520
No further questions, Your Honor.

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:29.970
The court will declare a recess and will resume after...

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:43.430
lunch. Can't stand it. It's not right. We've got to let the cat out of the bag. But Tom,

00:23:43.970 --> 00:23:58.470
you swore. What about Crazy Joe? Think what he'd do to us. Your Honor, in our remarks at the opening

00:23:58.470 --> 00:23:59.970
of this trial, we said...

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:05.890
that it was our purpose to prove that our client did this fearful deed while under-influenced

00:24:05.890 --> 00:24:12.800
drink. We have changed our mind. We will not enter this plea. I call Thomas Sawyer to

00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:28.980
the stand. You solemnly swear to tell the truth, the whole truth, and nothing but the

00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:29.980
truth, so help you God.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.660
Uh, I do.

00:24:38.400 --> 00:24:43.870
Thomas Sawyer, where were you on the 17th of June, about the hour of midnight?

00:24:45.320 --> 00:24:49.370
I was, uh, I was in the graveyard.

00:24:50.380 --> 00:24:53.320
Little bit louder, please. Don't be afraid.

00:24:54.280 --> 00:24:56.600
In the graveyard? You happy now?

00:24:56.990 --> 00:24:59.650
Were you anywhere near Haas Williams' grave?

00:25:00.250 --> 00:25:00.670
Yes, sir.

00:25:01.170 --> 00:25:01.930
Anyone with you?

00:25:02.720 --> 00:25:03.220
Yes, sir.

00:25:03.770 --> 00:25:06.510
We will produce your companion at the proper time.

00:25:07.580 --> 00:25:10.380
Why were you there in the graveyard at midnight?

00:25:10.930 --> 00:25:11.930
Do I have to say?

00:25:12.630 --> 00:25:13.510
Speak up, my boy.

00:25:14.310 --> 00:25:15.730
Never be ashamed of the truth.

00:25:17.510 --> 00:25:20.980
Um, to cure warts?

00:25:28.320 --> 00:25:29.960
Now, tell us what you're doing.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:39.670
what you saw that night? I saw. I saw the murder, but it wasn't Mutt Potter, did it? And who, my boy?

00:25:42.820 --> 00:25:59.210
It was Crazy Joe. He jumped in with that knife, and he... I'm a dead dog. What's that?

00:26:02.080 --> 00:26:04.180
If I could just get a closer look.

00:26:14.420 --> 00:26:17.970
I mean, hey, curiosity killed the cat, not the dog, right?

00:26:22.690 --> 00:26:23.920
Oh, hi there!

00:26:24.200 --> 00:26:26.700
I'm a ghost dog just checking up on this grave.

00:26:28.060 --> 00:26:28.860
Away from him!

00:26:29.540 --> 00:26:29.900
Don't hurt!

00:26:30.090 --> 00:26:30.370
My dog!
